## SQ-RE-45 | forge:milk fluid and item tags; nut milk bottle fills and drains at 250 mB (Item Drain live)
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest tag fluid forge:milk`; `/cdevtest tag item forge:milk`; `/cdevtest tag item creativedelight:milk_buckets`; `/cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:createfilling/nut_milk` and `createemptying/nut_milk`; an Item Drain given a Nut Milk bottle, `/cdevtest tickwarp 100`, `/cdevtest tank`
@pass fluid tag lists `minecraft:milk`, `hearthandharvest:goat_milk`, `creativedelight:nut_milk`; item tag `forge:milk` holds the three wooden milk buckets; `creativedelight:milk_buckets` holds `minecraft:milk_bucket` and the wooden milk buckets; filling and emptying recipes exist; the drain tank holds 250 mB nut milk
@fails `milk.js` tags and `R.createBottle(i.nut_milk_bottle, ...)` (needs Vintage Delight); the nut milk fluid in CD startup `fluids.js`; `hearthandharvest/tags.js` for goat milk
@absent creativedelight:milk_buckets (an item tag added 2026-11-21, not a registry id)
> forceload add 5264 5200 5279 5215
> fill 5264 -61 5200 5279 -61 5215 minecraft:stone
> fill 5264 -60 5200 5279 -56 5215 minecraft:air
sleep 2
> cdevtest tag fluid forge:milk
expect verb=tag kind=fluid tag=forge:milk n=\d+ ids=(?=\S*minecraft:milk\b)(?=\S*hearthandharvest:goat_milk\b)(?=\S*creativedelight:nut_milk\b)
> cdevtest tag item forge:milk
expect verb=tag kind=item tag=forge:milk n=\d+ ids=(?=\S*creativedelight:wooden_milk_bucket)(?=\S*creativedelight:wooden_goat_milk_bucket)(?=\S*creativedelight:wooden_nut_milk_bucket)
> cdevtest tag item creativedelight:milk_buckets
expect verb=tag kind=item tag=creativedelight:milk_buckets n=\d+ ids=(?=\S*minecraft:milk_bucket)(?=\S*creativedelight:wooden_milk_bucket)
> cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:createfilling/nut_milk
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:createfilling/nut_milk serializer=create:filling result=vintagedelight:nut_milk_bottle\*1
> cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:createemptying/nut_milk
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:createemptying/nut_milk serializer=create:emptying
> setblock 5265 -60 5201 create:item_drain
> cdevtest use 5265 -60 5201 held=vintagedelight:nut_milk_bottle face=up
> cdevtest tickwarp 100
waitlog verb=tickwarp .*end=done 60
> cdevtest tank 5265 -60 5201
expect verb=tank tanks=\d+ fluids=0:creativedelight:nut_milk\*250/
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look the emptying recipe's part=fields line shows 250 mB nut milk out of one bottle

## SQ-RE-46 | milk recipes take any milk: heated coffee mixing, Kettle once per milk, wooden buckets in milk recipes, golden milk bucket stays iron only
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:createmixing/milk_coffee`; `rdetail` the three hot cocoa Kettle ids (`farmersrespitebrewing/hot_cocoa`, `_goat_milk`, `_nut_milk`); `/cdevtest uses creativedelight:wooden_milk_bucket max=400`, the same for the wooden goat milk bucket; `/cdevtest uses minecraft:milk_bucket max=400`; `rdetail hostiledelight:mbutterrecp`
@pass milk coffee is a heated `create:mixing` taking `#forge:milk`; three `farmersrespite:brewing` hot cocoa recipes; the wooden milk buckets are used by Farmer's Delight cooking recipes, Hostile Delight's magical butter and Canned Powdered Milk, never by a Golden Milk Bucket recipe; the iron milk bucket still makes the Golden Milk Bucket
@fails `drinks.js` `milk()` (`R.createFluidTag(f.t_milk, 250)`); `kettle.js` MILKS base list (NCH `frBrewing` base array); `milk.js` `replaceInput` list; the Canned Powdered Milk row in `tools/gen_can_types.py` (rerun the generator); golden.js must keep `i.minecraft_milk_bucket`
@absent creativedelight:wooden_goat_milk_bucket (registered by the Creative Delight jar of 2026-11-21, after the last /dumpall); hostiledelight:mbutterrecp (a recipe id)
> cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:createmixing/milk_coffee
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:createmixing/milk_coffee serializer=create:mixing
> cdevtest rdetail creativedelight:farmersrespitebrewing/hot_cocoa
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:farmersrespitebrewing/hot_cocoa serializer=farmersrespite:brewing result=farmersdelight:hot_cocoa\*1
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:farmersrespitebrewing/hot_cocoa_goat_milk serializer=farmersrespite:brewing
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:farmersrespitebrewing/hot_cocoa_nut_milk serializer=farmersrespite:brewing
> cdevtest uses creativedelight:wooden_milk_bucket max=400
expect verb=uses id=\S+ serializer=farmersdelight:cooking
expect verb=uses id=hostiledelight:mbutterrecp\b
expect verb=uses id=\S*canned_powdered_milk\b
reject verb=uses id=\S*golden_milk_bucket
> cdevtest uses creativedelight:wooden_goat_milk_bucket max=400
expect verb=uses id=\S*canned_powdered_milk\b
> cdevtest uses minecraft:milk_bucket max=400
expect verb=uses id=\S*golden_milk_bucket\b
> cdevtest rdetail hostiledelight:mbutterrecp
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look milk_coffee's part=fields (or the ingredients) names the `forge:milk` fluid tag and the heat requirement `heated`; the three hot cocoa recipes differ only in the base fluid (milk, goat milk, nut milk)

## SQ-RE-47 | Slice & Dice mixer copies of milk pot recipes take the tag (no mixin error)
@group A
@commands Boot log; `/cdevtest recipes sliceanddice max=400`
@pass no mixin error naming `SliceAndDiceMilkTagMixin` in latest.log (it is `require = 0`, so a success prints nothing); Slice & Dice recipes are listed; the JEI check of a hot cocoa mixer copy with goat milk is CQ-RE-02
@fails `mixin/sliceanddice/SliceAndDiceMilkTagMixin` target `LazyMixingRecipe.resolve` moved in the Slice & Dice jar (the redirect silently not applied: compare the class in the jar)
bootreject (?i)mixin.*SliceAndDiceMilkTagMixin.*(fail|error|exception|not found)
> cdevtest recipes sliceanddice max=400
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
look the recipes summary line (n=) is above 0 or says why S&D builds its mixer copies lazily (then the JEI half of CQ-RE-02 is the only check)

